Subject: [DIAGNOSTIC] firmware: arm_scmi: test mailbox performance writes on A14

Target source: linux-msm/laptops-kernel
Revision: 51231839d5ef007638bd1c3500e6a76b337a66f3

On the tested A14, policy6 writes indices 4 / 20 / 4 via fast channels,
while frequency reads stay at index 13 and CPU6 AMU average stays near
3.434 GHz. No normal performance-message transfers occur in the trace.

Keep fast-channel reads, limits, level conversion and OPPs unchanged.
Skip mapping the performance-level SET fast channel. The existing
mailbox setter is then selected, and fast_switch_possible returns false
so cpufreq uses its slow path. The existing DT polling workaround applies
to these regular messages.

This diagnostic defaults on in this patched kernel. For a boot-time A/B
comparison, scmi_module.a14_perf_mailbox_set=0 retains the original path.
The parameter is read-only after boot because mapping happens at probe.

Mailbox success/failure and actual clock response still require testing
on the laptop. This is not an established upstream fix.

--- a/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/arm_scmi/perf.c
@@ -28,6 +28,12 @@
 #define SCMI_PROTOCOL_SUPPORTED_VERSION		0x40000
 
 #define MAX_OPPS		64
+
+/* Diagnostic for the A14: retain FC reads but acknowledge level writes. */
+static bool a14_perf_mailbox_set = true;
+module_param(a14_perf_mailbox_set, bool, 0444);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(a14_perf_mailbox_set,
+		"A14 diagnostic: send performance level writes through SCMI messages");
 
 enum scmi_performance_protocol_cmd {
 	PERF_DOMAIN_ATTRIBUTES = 0x3,
@@ -844,12 +850,22 @@
 				   &fc[PERF_FC_LIMIT].get_addr, NULL,
 				   &fc[PERF_FC_LIMIT].rate_limit);
 
-	if (dom->info.set_perf)
+	/*
+	 * Leave set_addr NULL to select the existing mailbox setter and make
+	 * scmi_fast_switch_possible() return false. Keep fast-channel reads:
+	 * this test changes only how performance level writes reach firmware.
+	 */
+	if (dom->info.set_perf && !a14_perf_mailbox_set)
 		ph->hops->fastchannel_init(ph, PERF_DESCRIBE_FASTCHANNEL,
 					   PERF_LEVEL_SET, 4, dom->id,
 					   &fc[PERF_FC_LEVEL].set_addr,
 					   &fc[PERF_FC_LEVEL].set_db,
 					   &fc[PERF_FC_LEVEL].rate_limit);
+
+	if (dom->info.set_perf && a14_perf_mailbox_set)
+		dev_info(ph->dev,
+			 "A14-SCMI: domain %u PERF_LEVEL_SET uses mailbox; fast switching disabled\n",
+			 dom->id);
 
 	if (dom->set_limits)
 		ph->hops->fastchannel_init(ph, PERF_DESCRIBE_FASTCHANNEL,
